.TH ACC-PKG 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-pkg \- build, sign, publish, install and query ACC role packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-pkg
.RB [ \-\-quiet ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-pkg
is the toolchain for ACC role packages (\fI.accpkg\fR): signed archives
carrying roles, skills, MCP definitions, evals and golden prompts.
Its query verbs are modelled on
.BR rpm (8)
(\fBqf\fR, \fBql\fR, \fBqi\fR, \fBqv\fR) and its build and scaffold verbs on
.BR rpmbuild (8).
.PP
Installation verifies the package signature before anything is unpacked:
keypair mode with a cosign public key (\fB\-\-key\fR), or keyless mode
against a Sigstore bundle (\fB\-\-issuer\fR, \fB\-\-subject\fR).
An unsigned package is refused unless \fB\-\-allow\-unsigned\fR is given,
which is logged as an audit event.
An Enterprise Contract policy, when present, is evaluated before the install
is committed.
.PP
.B acc-pkg
never prompts; it is built for CI and automation.
It is the package toolchain;
.BR acc-cli (1)
drives a running collective.
.SH OPTIONS
These sit before the command and apply to every command.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error standard output.
The \fB\-\-allow\-unsigned\fR audit line still prints.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON for the commands that produce data.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
The commands below are generated from the parser of this release.
.\" @COMMANDS@
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACC_PACKAGES_ROOT
Where packages are installed and queried (default \fB/var/lib/acc/packages\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_SYSTEM_CATALOG
The system catalog list (default \fB/etc/acc/catalogs.yaml\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_USER_CATALOG
The per-user catalog list (default \fB~/.acc/catalogs.yaml\fR).
.TP
.B COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY
Private key for keypair signing in \fBpublish\fR when \fB\-\-key\fR is not given.
.TP
.BR SIGSTORE_ID_TOKEN ", " SIGSTORE_OIDC_ISSUER
The OIDC token and issuer for keyless signing; \fBacc\-pkg login\fR reports
whether they are usable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/acc/packages
The installed packages and their registry.
.TP
.I /etc/acc/catalogs.yaml
The catalogs \fBlist \-\-available\fR and the resolver read.
.TP
.I /etc/acc/policy/enterprise\-contract.yaml
The default Enterprise Contract policy for \fBinstall\fR and \fBverify\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
User or argument error: missing file, bad arguments, unsafe path, already installed.
.TP
.B 2
Manifest schema failure, validation or lint errors.
.TP
.B 3
Dependency resolution failure, or an uninstall refused because something
still depends on the package.
.TP
.B 4
Content hash mismatch (tampering or corruption).
.TP
.B 5
Signature missing or rejected.
.TP
.B 6
Enterprise Contract policy violation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
acc\-pkg init my_role \-\-scope @you \-\-domain finance
acc\-pkg validate ./my_role
acc\-pkg build ./my_role \-o dist/my_role.accpkg
acc\-pkg publish dist/my_role.accpkg \-\-catalog\-url https://catalog.example/
acc\-pkg install dist/my_role.accpkg \-\-key cosign.pub
acc\-pkg list \-\-available
acc\-pkg qf \-\-kind role coding_agent    # which package provides a role
acc\-pkg qv                              # re-check every installed hash
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acc (1),
.BR acc-cli (1),
.BR acc-catalog (1),
.BR cosign (1)
